// =============================================================================
// SaaS platform Prisma fragment: SubscriptionNotice
// =============================================================================
//
// REFERENCE SNIPPET — see 01-subscription.prisma for conventions.
//
// One row per notice a subscriber is due — that a newer version of their plan is
// offered to them, that the version they are on is being retired, that their
// data is about to be deleted, and the others `SubscriptionNoticeKind` names —
// each told once. The platform records a notice before it has the
// application send it and confirms it after, so the unique key below is what
// makes a notice once — however many instances run the job — and the row is
// what shows later when it went out, to whom and how.
//
// A run takes a notice on by setting `claimedAt`, and lets it go again where the
// sending failed; a claim older than a quarter of an hour counts as abandoned.
// `deliveredAt`, `recipients` and `channel` are set together, when the
// application confirms it sent the notice.
//
// The record is evidence of what a subscriber was told, and outlives the
// subscription like the subscriber's account does (ADR 0012): `tenantId` and
// `subscriptionId` are kept as values, not as keys.
//
// `kind` is text holding a closed set, the kinds `SubscriptionNoticeKind` in
// @saasicat/core names; a row holding any other value is refused when it is
// read back. Text rather than an enum, so a kind added in a release needs no
// migration.
//
// Adopt it wherever `tenantBilling` is on: the start is refused without a place
// to keep notices, unless `tenantBilling.notices.record` names one of the
// application's own. Only an installation that serves no tenants leaves it out.
//
// Contract: @saasicat/core (SubscriptionNoticeRepository).

model SubscriptionNotice {
    id             String @id @default(uuid())
    tenantId       String
    subscriptionId String

    kind    String
    // What the notice is about, one per kind — for version-offered, the id of
    // the version offered; for version-retired, the id of the version retired,
    // so a subscription is told of a version's retirement once; for
    // deletion-reminder, the end's id and the lead time, so an end is reminded
    // once per lead time. `SubscriptionNoticeKey.subject` names each kind's.
    subject String
    // The notice as it was last handed to the application.
    content Json

    createdAt   DateTime  @default(now())
    claimedAt   DateTime?
    deliveredAt DateTime?
    // Who it went to and how, in the application's own terms.
    recipients  Json?
    channel     String?

    @@unique([subscriptionId, kind, subject])
    @@index([kind, subject])
    @@map("subscription_notices")
}
